00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:04.999 align:start position:0%
a massive document release overnight is  shedding new light on the 1963  assassination of President John F  Kennedy the National Archives put out  thousands of government files from one  of America's most traumatic periods at  the last minute President Trump said he  had to block the release of hundreds of  records the FBI and CIA claimed those  secret documents could pose a security  risk CBS News had a team up all night  reading the Declassified papers to see  what they reveal chip Reid is at the  National Archives in Washington with  what we have learned  chip good morning well good morning  according to a 1992 law last night at  midnight was the deadline for releasing  the last batch of documents pertaining  to the Kennedy assassination now some  documents have been withheld for now for  National Security Review but that still  leaves us tens of thousands of pages to  read what happened that November day in  Dallas still haunts the nation a young  president killed President Kennedy died  at 1:00 p.m. Central Standard Time  then the alleged assassin Lee Harvey  Oswald was killed two days later  stirring rumors of a conspiracy but the  newly released documents show the FBI  knew of a possible threat against Oswald  FBI director J Edgar Hoover wrote a memo  saying the night before Oswald was shot  a man called saying he was a member of a  committee organized to kill Oswald the  FBI reportedly contacted Dallas Police  who assured them adequate protection  would be given however this was not done  the FBI had actually been monitoring  Oswald's shooter Jack Ruby for a year  Hoover wrote that he was concerned about  conspiracies and wanted to have  something issued so we can convince the  public that Oswald is the real assassin  the FBI director also knew that Oswald  had ties to Cuba and Russia  Oswald was revealed to be on the FBI's  radar a month before the assassination  and he apparently told an associate that  he wanted to kill President Eisenhower  some information that came out after the  assassination one man told investigators  he heard a man betting $100 that Prez  Kennedy would be dead within three weeks  a 413 page memo details every threat  against Kennedy including those from the  Ku Klux Klan and some with mental  illness the documents also show that  both Russia and Cuba feared they would  be blamed and Russia worried that  Kennedy's death could possibly lead to  nuclear war experts on the Kennedy  assassination say there are so many  newly released documents and so many of  them are cryptic and almost impossible  to understand that it could be weeks  months or even years before we  understand their full significance and  even then they say we may never know the  whole truth  Charlie thanks chip
 

